    "created_at": "2022-02-15T15:53:18Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-02-15T15:53:18Z",
    "body": "I would like to know whether there are existing use cases that require unrendered fallback content to be interactive (focus + keyboard input). Currently this is partially broken in Blink-based browsers, but practically no-one seems to care (since HitRegions were abandoned), so those bugs are not getting any attention. \r\n\r\nUnless I am missing something, It seems to me like DOM elements that overlap the canvas (without being children of the canvas element) are largely sufficient for supporting interaction and accessibility use cases. So I would like to suggest removing the requirement that unrendered fallback content be interactive.\r\n\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
